# Pairs with RAllOrNothing, and shows that a receiver reader observing
# BETWEEN two prepare arrivals is in scope: RAllOrNothing is a state
# invariant, so it is checked in every state, including each one between two
# re-shipped prepares. #4482's intended receiver design is applied (the export
# ships a decision row for every saga the origin stores; the receiver's prepare
# seam settles a re-shipped pre-cut prepare against it, materialised on
# Committed and dropped on Aborted; pre-cut records are re-shipped). The
# defect is in the export: a decided saga whose buckets have not drained yet
# is exported with its decision row but without committed rows for those
# buckets, so the receiver serves every key pre-saga under a committed
# decision. Each re-shipped prepare then settles its OWN key post-saga as a
# last-writer-wins write, and a reader between two arrivals sees one key
# post-saga and the other pre-saga. Exporting such a saga's resident buckets as
# committed rows (the base's ExportRow) is what keeps the settle atomic.
# The omission is keyed to a saga NONE of whose buckets has drained, where
# every key is otherwise pre-saga, so the counterexample is the key-by-key
# window rather than a partial snapshot.
MODULE: RAllOrNothingSettleKeyByKey
TARGET: RAllOrNothing
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a decided saga's undrained buckets are exported without committed rows, so re-shipped prepares settle it one key at a time
PERTURBS: Bootstrap, DeliverPrepare

--- FIND
    IF snap = "committed" THEN "post"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no committed rows for a decided saga none of whose buckets has drained.
    IF snap = "committed" THEN (IF \A j \in XKeys : pend[T][j] = "pending" THEN "pre" ELSE "post")
--- END
--- FIND
    /\ \E snap \in Snap0 :
         /\ rproj' = [k \in XKeys |-> ExportRow(snap, k)]
         /\ rpend' = [k \in XKeys |-> IF ExportsPrepared(snap, k) THEN "pending" ELSE "none"]
    /\ outbox' = {}
    /\ rconn' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, dlv, rterm, registryVars, barrierVars>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ \E snap \in Snap0 :
         /\ rproj' = [k \in XKeys |-> ExportRow(snap, k)]
         /\ rpend' = [k \in XKeys |-> IF ExportsPrepared(snap, k) THEN "pending" ELSE "none"]
\* MUTATION: the export's decision row is recorded on the receiver.
         /\ rdec' = [rdec EXCEPT !["A"] = IF snap \in {"committed", "aborted"} THEN snap ELSE rdec["A"]]
\* MUTATION: any pre-cut record still retained is shipped again.
    /\ outbox' \in SUBSET outbox
    /\ rconn' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, dlv, rterm, rarr, rexp, rout, rstage, rdeleg, rdial, barrierVars>>
--- END
--- FIND
    /\ rpend' = IF rterm[m.key] = "none" THEN [rpend EXCEPT ![m.key] = "pending"] ELSE rpend
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, rconn, rterm, rproj, registryVars, barrierVars>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a prepare is settled by txid against the recorded decision.
    /\ rpend' = IF rterm[m.key] = "none" /\ rdec[TreeOf(m.key)] = "inflight" THEN [rpend EXCEPT ![m.key] = "pending"] ELSE rpend
    /\ rproj' = IF rdec[TreeOf(m.key)] = "committed" THEN [rproj EXCEPT ![m.key] = "post"] ELSE rproj
    /\ UNCHANGED <<originVars, xtree, oext, orcv, rconn, rterm, registryVars, barrierVars>>
--- END
--- FIND
    IF forgotten[T] THEN {"indeterminate", "inflight"} ELSE {Origin!RegistryView(T)}
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a stored aged-out row exports its recorded verdict.
    IF forgotten[T] THEN {decision[T]} ELSE {Origin!RegistryView(T)}
--- END
